                <pb facs="0622" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2376: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-21T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                                1919, 7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            August 21, 1.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Asia Banking Corporation has made a contract for a loan of $500,000 with the
                    Hupeh Provincial Government, with Central Government sanction and guarantee
                    security income of provincial mint, purpose not stated. Japanese bank claims
                    option [on] all Hupeh loans. Provincial Government considers Japanese terms too
                    high. Should the Legation approve?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
